       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled prescription dose of ibuprofen for adults. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day, usually given as 800 mg up to four times daily. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and there is no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), which is typical for pain.\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily. This may be where the \"1600\" came from.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note. I'd still recommend confirming it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
