       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the dosing problem. I can't verify the indication, and I know of no adult condition where ibuprofen 6,400 mg/day is appropriate. It's twice the labeled maximum, and the extra dose adds toxicity risk without added benefit. You also haven't named the condition or the treatment stage.\n\nThese options would let me move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or less if you want a lower dose. I can enter that now.\n- **Get pharmacy or attending sign-off first.** If a specialist protocol really calls for a supra-maximal dose, a pharmacist or the responsible attending should review and approve it. Their approval or a protocol reference can then go in the order note. Your institution may also require an override pathway outside this tool.\n- **Check the dose.** If the number came from a note, a protocol, or a different drug, it's worth a second look.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
